From: Lars Wikman <lars@underjord.io>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: rover: give Venus its firmware memory

msm8937.dtsi leaves venus_mem disabled, so the region was never
reserved and Venus failed its probe at the memory-region lookup, before
it looked for firmware. Enable it, at 6 MiB: the driver's limit, and
room for the msm8937 family's images.

The watch ships no Venus firmware (stock Wear OS leaves video out), but
its TrustZone takes another msm8937 phone's; ticwatch-bringup says
where it goes.

Signed-off-by: Lars Wikman <lars@underjord.io>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm429w-mobvoi-rover.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm429w-mobvoi-rover.dts
@@ -710,6 +710,17 @@ &usb_hs_phy {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * Venus, the video codec. The watch ships no firmware for it (stock leaves
+ * video out), so it runs one from the same family. msm8937.dtsi leaves its
+ * carve-out disabled; the images that fit take up to 5 MiB, so give it the
+ * 6 MiB the driver allows.
+ */
+&venus_mem {
+	size = <0x0 0x600000>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &xo_board {
 	clock-frequency = <19200000>;
 };
-- 
